<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Medical and scientific writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical & scientific writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical writing"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/scientific-writing/"}>{"Scientific writing"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/medical-writing/editorial-quality-support-service/"}>{"Editorial quality"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/medico-legal-support-services/"}>{"Medico-legal"}</a></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the document "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"}>{"Medical & scientific writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Editorial and Quality Support"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Editorial and Quality Support Service"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"“Editing” is sold as one thing and is at least five, priced fourfold apart, and no two suppliers use the same names for them. That is why two honest quotes for the same manuscript can differ by a factor of four, and why authors routinely buy a proofread when they needed a restructure. Pubrica’s editorial and quality support is independent checking of documents written elsewhere — by you, by your team or by another supplier — at a level we name before we quote, against the reporting guideline your design requires and the ethical standards your journal applies. We will tell you which level you actually need, including when the answer is a cheaper one than you asked for."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#eq-lvl"}>{"Find your editing level"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"Five levels, one word"}</b>{" · what each actually covers"}</span> <span>{"Our rate, per word"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Proofreading"}</b><span>{"$0.025"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "14%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Copyediting"}</b><span>{"$0.035"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "30%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Line editing"}</b><span>{"$0.050"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "50%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Substantive editing"}</b><span>{"$0.075"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "76%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Developmental editing"}</b><span>{"$0.100"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Read it"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" name the level "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" quote "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" edit "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"second reader"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every document"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"The level named before the quote"}</li> <li>{"A style sheet built and handed over"}</li> <li>{"References opened, not matched"}</li> <li>{"Read by a second person"}</li> <li>{"Acknowledged, never ghosted"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $150"}</b><span>{"A proofread of 6,000 words. $450 for a substantive edit of the same"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Editorial and quality support for authors, institutions and publishers"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ICMJE · COPE · GPP 2022"}</b><span>{"With CONSORT 2025, PRISMA 2020, STROBE and CARE by design"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-what-we-do-3b1prn"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-who-we-serve-1txmya9"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-our-compliance-ks0ea6"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-how-it-works-16s41jj"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-our-experts-1lotauu"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-sample-work-1a7rm2q"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-packages-1adzr7j"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-guarantee-1jjfynq"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-client-stories-1exnw4j"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-editorial-quality-support-faq-1r4unno"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-what-we-do-3b1prn"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Eight bodies of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most documents need two or three. Buying the ones you need is cheaper than buying a tier built around them, which is why the chooser above prices a level rather than a package."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Scientific and substantive editing"}</b> <span>{"Structure, argument and the order the claims arrive in; whether the introduction narrows to one question; whether the methods describe what was actually done; whether every number in the text matches the table it came from; and whether each claim in the discussion is supported by the result it rests on. The level most often needed and the one least often bought."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Language and line editing"}</b> <span>{"Sentence by sentence, for clarity, flow and register — in your voice rather than flattened into house prose, which is the failure mode of cheap editing and the thing authors writing in an additional language most often complain about afterwards. Grammar, usage and punctuation corrected alongside rather than billed twice."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Reporting-guideline compliance"}</b> <span>{"Every item of the guideline your design requires located in the text by page and line, or recorded as missing — at the version current this month rather than the one in the template. CONSORT and SPIRIT both changed in April 2025, and a manuscript built on a 2010 flow diagram is reporting to a document its own successor has withdrawn."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Ethical and authorship review"}</b> <span>{"Authorship against the four ICMJE criteria, contributions in CRediT, competing interests, funding, ethics and consent statements, data availability measured against what the ethics approval actually permits, and GPP 2022 where the research is company-sponsored. Uncomfortable conversations are much cheaper before publication than after."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Similarity screening, read rather than scored"}</b> <span>{"We run the report and read every match: which are properly quoted and cited, which need a citation added, which are your own earlier writing and need handling as text recycling under COPE’s 2024 position, and which are a real problem. "}<b>{"We do not sell similarity reduction"}</b>{" — rewording a passage to lower a number without fixing the attribution is the same failure in different words."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Reference and citation verification"}</b> <span>{"Every reference opened and read against the statement it supports rather than matched to the citation, and checked for retraction, expression of concern and indexing. No reference manager warns you that a paper you cited was retracted eighteen months ago. Over a third of references in medical journal articles carry some inaccuracy, which is a Cochrane finding rather than a sales line."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Formatting and submission preparation"}</b> <span>{"Journal house style, reference style in AMA, APA, Vancouver, Harvard, MLA or Chicago, figure and table specification, supplementary files, and the declarations pack. Detailed on our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/manuscript-formatting"} data-nav={""}>{"manuscript formatting"}</a>{" and "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/journal-submission"} data-nav={""}>{"journal submission"}</a>{" pages, and included in the levels above where the document needs it."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Independent QC of another supplier’s work"}</b> <span>{"Frequently the most useful thing on this page. Send us something you paid somebody else to write or edit and we will tell you what was done, what was not, and whether the level you were charged for is the level you received. We will also say where the previous work was sound, which is more often than the pitch for this service would suggest."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-who-we-serve-1txmya9"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions editorial and quality support."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of client, and one shared position: somebody else wrote the document, and it now has to be right."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Researchers and academics"}</b><span>{"Usually at the point where the draft is finished, the co-authors have stopped reading it properly, and the deadline is next week. The commonest request is a proofread and the commonest need is a level or two above it."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Clinicians and healthcare professionals"}</b><span>{"Writing alongside a caseload, where the constraint is uninterrupted hours rather than ability. Case reports, audits and observational work, checked against the guideline the journal will screen with."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Authors writing in an additional language"}</b><span>{"The largest group buying this service, and the one the market serves worst — sold flattening into house prose, sold similarity reduction they do not need, and sold AI-detection reassurance that no tool can honestly give. We edit in your voice and say what the checks can establish."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Universities, departments and research offices"}</b><span>{"Standing arrangements across a cohort, editorial support inside an existing process, and QC of work produced elsewhere. Where a university’s regulations define what help is permitted, we work inside them and document what was done."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical, biotechnology and device companies"}</b><span>{"Independent QC of documents written internally or by another vendor, with version currency on every standard cited and claims checked for agreement across the document set. Under GPP 2022 where the research is company-sponsored."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Publishers and journals"}</b><span>{"Overflow copyediting and proofreading to your own style guide and workflow, with a style sheet per title rather than per project, and a named editor who stays with the title."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"What we do not do, and who should"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"We do not guarantee journal acceptance, and that sentence appears on every page of this site. We do not sell similarity reduction: we read the report and tell you what it means, and where a passage needs a citation we say so rather than rewording it to lower a number. We do not sell an AI-detection clearance, because no detector is reliable enough for one to be honest and the published false-positive rates fall hardest on the authors who would buy it. We do not issue editing certificates as evidence of anything — no publisher we could find requires one, accepts one as bearing on a decision, or rejects a paper for lacking one, and the “Scopus-accepted” and “Web of Science ready” certificates advertised in this market correspond to no scheme either organisation operates. We will confirm in writing exactly what we did, which is the thing that is actually useful, and which your institution may require. We are not peer reviewers: we check that a document reports what it should and claims what it can support, not whether the science is right. And we do not edit assessed work where an institution’s regulations prohibit assistance, whoever is asking."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-our-compliance-ks0ea6"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six frameworks, with the versions current on 21 September 2026."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"An editorial service is judged on whether it knows which document governs what. Three of these have moved in the last two years, and one of them is the point this page opens with."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds stds--3"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE Recommendations"}>{"ICMJE"}<em>{"Jan 2026"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICMJE Recommendations "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(updated January 2026)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The "}<b>{"four authorship criteria"}</b>{" are unchanged and all four must be met by every author. The January 2026 update added a new "}<b>{"Section V"}</b>{" on the use of artificial intelligence in publishing, split between authors, reviewers and editors, and a new "}<b>{"Section III.L.2"}</b>{" requiring that all authors be able to review the data supporting the results. It is also the document that governs our own position: “writing assistance, technical editing, language editing, and proofreading” do not confer authorship. We are acknowledged, never listed. One practical note — the PDF carries the January 2026 text while icmje.org’s HTML pages still showed January 2024 when we checked, so cite the PDF."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"COPE"}>{"COPE"}<em>{"core practices"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"COPE "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(and the two positions that matter here)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Two COPE documents govern most of what this service does. On similarity: COPE “does not recommend using a specific percentage of duplication or overlap as a benchmark for conducting an investigation” — so there is no threshold to hit, whatever an editing service tells you. On reusing your own earlier writing: the COPE position on "}<b>{"handling text recycling"}</b>{", version 1 published 20 August 2024, defines it as reusing your own previous writing without being transparent or citing the original, and weighs the extent, the location in the paper and whether it was disclosed. Note that COPE’s older text-recycling document is authored by BioMed Central and carried as endorsed legacy guidance from 2016, not as COPE’s own position."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"GPP 2022"}>{"GPP"}<em>{"2022"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"GPP 2022 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(company-sponsored research)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Good Publication Practice for company-sponsored biomedical research, published in the "}<i>{"Annals of Internal Medicine"}</i>{" on "}<b>{"30 August 2022"}</b>{" and stewarded by ISMPP. It is the third update of the 2003 original, after GPP2 in 2009 and GPP3 in 2015, and it applies alongside the ICMJE criteria where a sponsor is involved. "}<b>{"GPP3 is superseded and there is no GPP4"}</b>{" — that was the working title during development, dropped when the guideline moved to year-based naming. You will see “GPP3/GPP4” listed as a standard. Do not confuse GPP 2022 with the "}<b>{"GPCAP 2026 update"}</b>{" published this year: that covers conference abstracts and presentations and is a different guideline."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Reporting guidelines"}>{"EQUATOR"}<em>{"by design"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Reporting guidelines "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(the version, not just the acronym)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}><b>{"CONSORT 2025"}</b>{" for trials and "}<b>{"SPIRIT 2025"}</b>{" for protocols, both published April 2025 and both stating that their predecessors should no longer be used. "}<b>{"PRISMA 2020"}</b>{" for systematic reviews, which despite its name appeared in 2021. "}<b>{"STROBE (2007)"}</b>{" for observational studies, still current. "}<b>{"STARD 2015"}</b>{", "}<b>{"TRIPOD+AI (2024)"}</b>{", "}<b>{"ARRIVE 2.0"}</b>{", "}<b>{"CHEERS 2022"}</b>{", "}<b>{"COREQ"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"SRQR"}</b>{", and "}<b>{"CARE"}</b>{" for case reports. A quality check that confirms a checklist exists is not a quality check; ours locates every item in the text by page and line, or records it as missing."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Editing standards"}>{"PES"}<em>{"2024 · CMOS · EFA"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"The editing standards "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(three, and they disagree)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"There is no single industry taxonomy of editing levels, and pretending otherwise is how buyers get sold the wrong one. "}<b>{"Editors Canada’s "}<i>{"Professional Editorial Standards"}</i>{" 2024"}</b>{" — note, not the 2016 edition — defines structural, stylistic, copy and proofreading standards over a foundational part. The "}<b>{"Chicago Manual of Style"}</b>{" splits manuscript editing into mechanical and substantive at 2.49 and 2.50, and treats line editing as a separate earlier pass at 2.53. The "}<b>{"Editorial Freelancers Association"}</b>{" names developmental, line, copyediting and proofreading, and defines proofreading comparatively — checking one stage against the previous — which is narrower than how the word is usually sold. We name which we mean, in all three vocabularies, before quoting."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Similarity and AI screening"}>{"SCREENING"}<em>{"what it proves"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Similarity and AI screening "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(and their documented limits)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Turnitin’s own guidance states that “plagiarism cannot be determined by the similarity score alone” and that there is "}<b>{"no single acceptable or perfect score"}</b>{". On AI detection, COPE’s September 2025 guidance says detection tools “should not be relied upon in isolation” and that none is fully accurate; Turnitin now publishes no headline accuracy figure, suppresses results below 20%, and states that a score “should not be used as the sole basis for adverse actions”. The evidence on bias is the part that matters to this service’s clients: seven detectors tested on human-written TOEFL essays produced an average "}<b>{"61.3% false-positive rate"}</b>{", while essays by native-English school students were classified almost perfectly. We run these checks and read the output; we do not sell a score."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"An assessor asks who decided. A tool cannot be the answer."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Regulatory documents are read by people whose job is to trace decisions back to evidence and to individuals. That makes provenance the binding constraint rather than speed, and a fluent sentence with no traceable source is worse than a clumsy one that has it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Finding source material across a document set. Consistency of terms, figures and cross-references between documents in a submission. Drafting highly templated sections that a writer then verifies line by line against source."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Anything entering a submission as drafted; clinical or benefit-risk interpretation; safety narratives; literature appraisal for a clinical evaluation; and any statement an assessor would expect to trace to a named, qualified individual."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders, regulators and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as an integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-how-it-works-16s41jj"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the editorial and quality support service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the first one is free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Because the most expensive mistake in this category is buying the wrong level, and neither of us can tell which level a document needs without reading some of it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"A sample edit, at no cost, before anything is agreed"}</h3> <p><b>{"Send the document and we edit 1,000 words of it for free."}</b>{" You see the level of intervention, the tone we take with your voice, and the kind of thing we query rather than change. We see whether the level you asked for is the level it needs. If it needs less, we say so and quote less; we lose money on that conversation often enough that it is worth telling you it happens."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"The level named, in writing, with what it excludes"}</h3> <p><b>{"Not “editing”."}</b>{" Proofreading, copyediting, line editing, substantive or developmental — named in the three published vocabularies so you can compare our quote against anybody else’s, with what that level does "}<i>{"not"}</i>{" cover stated explicitly. A quote that does not say what is excluded is a quote you cannot compare, and this market runs on that."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"A style sheet built before the editing starts"}</h3> <p><b>{"Every terminology decision, spelling variant, abbreviation and formatting convention recorded as it is made."}</b>{" It is what makes a long document internally consistent, it is what lets a second editor pick up a chapter without contradicting the first, and it is yours at the end — which is what makes the next paper from the same project cheaper. Most services skip it because it is invisible until it is missing."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Edited, with every change visible and every query answerable"}</h3> <p><b>{"Tracked changes, and comments where a change would alter meaning."}</b>{" We do not silently rewrite a claim: if a sentence says more than the results support, we query it, show you the estimate it rests on, and let you decide. An edit that quietly changes what a paper asserts is a worse problem than the one it fixed."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Checks that are not editing, run separately"}</h3> <p><b>{"References opened and read, and checked for retraction and indexing. Reporting checklist mapped. Declarations reviewed. Similarity report read rather than scored."}</b>{" These are separate passes because they find different things, and running them inside an edit is how a retracted reference survives to publication."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"A second reader, then the report"}</h3> <p><b>{"Read by somebody who did not do the editing."}</b>{" An editor re-reading their own work reads what they intended. You receive the edited document, the clean version, the style sheet, the query log with our reasoning, the reference log and the checklist — and a short note on what we did not do, and why, so nobody assumes a level of checking that was not bought."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send it. We will edit a thousand words free and name the level."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: a sample edit you can read, the level the document actually needs, the price, and an honest note on anything we found that editing will not fix. If the answer is that you need less than you asked for, that is what the note will say."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The document"}</b><span>{"In an editable format, not a PDF if you can help it"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The destination"}</b><span>{"The journal, funder or institution it is going to"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The rules"}</b><span>{"Instructions to authors, or your institution’s handbook"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The style"}</b><span>{"Any style guide or previous paper you want matched"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The deadline"}</b><span>{"And whether it is real or aspirational"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The history"}</b><span>{"Any previous decision letters or supervisor comments"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"A PDF is worth mentioning because it changes the price. Editing a PDF means either working in comments, which is slower and harder for you to accept, or converting it and reintroducing every layout decision by hand. If the editable original exists, sending it is the single cheapest thing you can do for this project."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Which level, and what it costs"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"You are probably about to buy the wrong level."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Tell the chooser what the document is, what is wrong with it and how long it is, and it names the level, prices it, and shows you what that level does "}<i>{"not"}</i>{" include — which is the part no quote tells you. It also gives the same level’s name under all three published taxonomies, because the Editorial Freelancers Association, the Chicago Manual of Style and Editors Canada do not agree, and that disagreement is why quotes are impossible to compare. Tick the similarity or AI boxes and it will tell you honestly what those checks can and cannot establish."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"eq-lvl"} data-tool={"edl"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"eq-lvl-body"}>{"Editing level chooser"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"The level you need, what it excludes, what it costs, and what a similarity score actually means."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"eq-lvl-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-eq-doc"}>{"What is the document?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"doc"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-eq-doc"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"art"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Journal manuscript"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"thesis"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Thesis or dissertation"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"grant"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Grant or proposal"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"reg"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Regulatory or clinical document"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"book"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Book chapter or report"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"How long is it?"}</span><input type={"number"} data-k={"wc"} value={"5000"} min={200} max={120000} step={100} /></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"What stage is it at?"}</span><select data-k={"stage"}><option value={"first"} selected={true}>{"First complete draft"}</option><option value={"rev"}>{"Revised after internal review"}</option><option value={"final"}>{"Final, about to submit"}</option><option value={"proofs"}>{"Typeset proofs from the publisher"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Who wrote it?"}</span><select data-k={"who"}><option value={"eal"} selected={true}>{"The authors, in English as an additional language"}</option><option value={"nat"}>{"The authors, native English speakers"}</option><option value={"sup"}>{"Another supplier"}</option><option value={"tr"}>{"A translator, from another language"}</option></select></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"st"} /><span>{"The structure or the argument is not working"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"sn"} checked={true} /><span>{"Sentences are hard to follow"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"gr"} checked={true} /><span>{"Grammar, spelling and usage need correcting"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"tm"} /><span>{"Terminology and abbreviations are inconsistent"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"rf"} /><span>{"References are incomplete or inconsistently styled"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"fm"} /><span>{"It needs formatting to a journal’s house style"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"fg"} /><span>{"Figures and tables need checking against the text"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"sim"} /><span>{"I am worried about a similarity or plagiarism score"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"aid"} /><span>{"I am worried about an AI-writing detector"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"Line editing"}</b><span>{"From $250 · 5–8 business days"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--hd trow--txt"}><b>{"Item"}</b><span>{"Detail"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"What this level does"}</b><span>{"Sentence by sentence: clarity, flow, register, paragraph order within a section, redundancy, hedging that hides a finding and overstatement that inflates one. Copyediting is included alongside it here rather than charged twice."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"What it does not do"}</b><span>{"It does not reorder sections, rebuild an argument or decide what the paper claims. If the problem is that the discussion argues something the results do not support, this is not the level that fixes it."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Journal manuscript"}</b><span>{"Edited against the target journal’s instructions to authors and the reporting guideline your design requires. Where no journal is chosen yet, we edit to a defensible general standard and reformat later, which is cheaper than editing twice."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Written by authors using English as an additional language"}</b><span>{"The disadvantage is documented — 38.1% of non-native speakers report a language-related rejection against 14.4% of native speakers, and 42.5% are routinely asked to improve their English during revision against 3.4% (Amano et al., "}<i>{"PLOS Biology"}</i>{" 2023). What follows is that language editing is worth buying, and that it is not a substitute for the level above it if the structure is the problem. We edit for clarity in your voice rather than flattening the paper into house prose."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"The price, worked"}</b><span>{"5,000 words at $0.050 a word, with a minimum of $240. For context: the Editorial Freelancers Association’s 2025 survey puts freelance medical copyediting at 3.0 to 5.0 cents a word and medical developmental editing at 5.3 to 6.8 cents — one editor, no project management, no second reader. Elsevier charges $0.10 a word for language editing alone at this length, and Wiley charges $0.25 a word above 6,000 words for its top tier. We sit between the two, which is where a service with a second reader and a published scope belongs. The figure is a starting point, not a quote: we read the document first and tell you if it needs a different level."}</span></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"The same level, under the three published taxonomies"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Editorial Freelancers Association"}</b><span>{"Line editing — work at sentence and paragraph level, on language and style."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Chicago Manual of Style"}</b><span>{"Chicago treats line editing as a pass "}<i>{"before"}</i>{" copyediting (2.53), not as a grander version of it — a distinction worth knowing when a supplier sells them as a ladder."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Editors Canada, PES 2024"}</b><span>{"Part C, Standards for Stylistic Editing."}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Why three names for one thing."}</b>{" There is no industry-standard taxonomy of editing levels, and that is not a quibble — it is why two quotes for “editing” can differ fourfold and both be honest. The EFA names four services; Chicago splits manuscript editing into mechanical and substantive and treats line editing as a separate earlier pass; Editors Canada’s Professional Editorial Standards 2024 defines four levels under different names again, over a foundational part that is not a level at all. They do not map onto each other. So before you compare prices, make the supplier tell you which of the five things above they are actually going to do — and if they will not, that is your answer."}</p></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"Sources, and a correction."}</b>{" Level definitions from the Editorial Freelancers Association’s editorial services definitions and 2025 rate survey, the Chicago Manual of Style 2.48–2.50 and 2.53, and Editors Canada’s "}<i>{"Professional Editorial Standards"}</i>{" 2024 — note that the 2016 edition is superseded. Similarity: Turnitin and iThenticate guidance pages; COPE, “Determining acceptable levels of plagiarism/duplication”; Elsevier PERK; Springer Nature’s Crossref Similarity Check guide for editors. Text recycling: COPE position, 20 August 2024. AI detection: Liang W, Yuksekgonul M, Mao Y, Wu E, Zou J, “GPT detectors are biased against non-native English writers”, "}<i>{"Patterns"}</i>{" 2023;4(7):100779; Turnitin’s own AI writing detection guidance; COPE, “Emerging AI dilemmas in scholarly publishing”, updated 17 September 2025. Language: Amano T et al., "}<i>{"PLOS Biology"}</i>{" 2023;21(7):e3002184. All checked 21 September 2026. "}<b>{"The correction:"}</b>{" “Good Publication Practice (GPP3/GPP4)” gets listed among the standards as though both editions were live. "}<b>{"GPP 2022 is the current guideline"}</b>{" — published in the "}<i>{"Annals of Internal Medicine"}</i>{" on 30 August 2022, stewarded by ISMPP, and the third update of the 2003 original after GPP2 in 2009 and GPP3 in 2015. There is no GPP4: that was the working title during development, and the guideline was renamed at publication. GPP3 is superseded. A supplier’s own guideline page will often say so correctly while the page selling the work does not, which is the kind of internal contradiction a careful reader finds first."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </div></section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-our-experts-1lotauu"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Scope, judgement, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, the reporting guideline"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"The applicable checklist"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, ICH E9"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on, and records it so somebody else could find it again. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-sample-work-1a7rm2q"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The editorial QC report, on somebody else’s edit."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The most useful thing this service does is tell you whether the level you paid for is the level you received. This is a real report on a manuscript that had already been through another provider’s top tier, brought to us because the authors could not tell what had actually been done to it. Use the tabs, then open the full report."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Editorial QC report"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Cohort study · 5,900 words · already edited elsewhere"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"Level delivered · language · checks · declarations"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the QC report"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"eq-t1"} aria-controls={"eq-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Level"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"eq-t2"} aria-controls={"eq-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Language"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"eq-t3"} aria-controls={"eq-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Checks"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"eq-t4"} aria-controls={"eq-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Declarations"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"eq-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"eq-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Sold as “premium scientific editing”. Delivered as a copyedit."}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"1,184 changes, of which 1,102 were spelling, punctuation, article use and tense. Eighty-two touched sentence structure. Nothing touched section order, the argument, or the relationship between the discussion and the results. That is a competent copyedit sold at four times a copyedit’s price, and the invoice named no level, which is how it was possible."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"No style sheet, and terminology drifted"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The same variable is called three things across the methods, results and discussion; two abbreviations are defined twice and one is never defined. A style sheet built at the start prevents all of this and takes an editor an hour. None was produced, and none was handed over."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A claim was silently broadened by the editor"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“was associated with” became “led to” in the abstract. It reads better. It also asserts causation from an observational cohort, which is the single objection this design always attracts. Changed back, with the reasoning recorded in the query log rather than made silently in the other direction."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The language work itself was good"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Worth saying plainly. Ninety-four per cent of the language changes were correct and we kept them. The problem was not the quality of the copyedit; it was that a copyedit was sold as something else and the authors had no way to tell."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Level charged: premium"}</span><span>{"Level delivered: copyediting"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"eq-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"eq-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“The results of our study demonstrate that the exposure led to a significant increase in the outcome.”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Returned to “Exposure was associated with a higher rate of the outcome (adjusted HR 1.34, 95% CI 1.09 to 1.65).” Three changes: the causal verb removed, the estimate put in the sentence rather than left in a table, and “significant” dropped because the interval says everything the word was doing."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A 74-word methods sentence left intact"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Grammatical, correctly punctuated, and containing four separate procedures. Split into three. A copyedit leaves this alone because it is not wrong; a line edit does not, because a reader cannot hold it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Hedging that hid the actual finding"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“It may possibly be suggested that there could be some indication of” — nine words of insulation in front of a result the data support. Reduced to the claim itself. Over-hedging costs authors more than overstatement does, because a reviewer reads it as a lack of confidence in your own work."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The authors’ voice kept"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Two of the four authors write in English as an additional language. The brief was clarity, not neutralisation. Where a construction is unusual and clear, it stayed — flattening a paper into house prose is a failure of editing, not a standard of it."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"310 further changes at line level"}</span><span>{"1,102 earlier corrections kept"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"eq-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"eq-t3"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"References opened and read"}</dt><dd>{"52. The previous provider had restyled all 52 and opened none — which is visible, because restyling propagates a wrong page range and reading does not."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Do not support the statement"}</dt><dd>{"3. Two inherited from another paper’s reference list; one supports the opposite direction of effect in the population at issue."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Retracted"}</dt><dd>{"1, retracted eleven months before this manuscript was drafted and cited in the introduction as current evidence. Nothing in a reference manager, a copyedit or a similarity report catches this. It has to be checked deliberately."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Similarity report"}</dt><dd>{"Delivered by the previous provider as a number and a colour. We read all 34 matches: 26 were correctly quoted and cited methods text, 5 were the authors’ own earlier methods section and needed citing as text recycling, 2 needed a citation added, 1 was a real attribution problem in the introduction. The number itself told the authors nothing, which is what Turnitin says it is for."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reporting checklist"}</dt><dd>{"STROBE, not previously completed. Twenty-two items located by page and line; four incomplete, all four answerable from what the team already held."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Numbers against tables"}</dt><dd>{"Every figure in the text checked against its table. Two mismatches, both in the abstract, both introduced during an earlier revision rather than by the editor."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"eq-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"eq-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Authorship"}</dt><dd>{"Five listed. One met only the first ICMJE criterion — data collection, no drafting, no approval recorded, no accountability. Moved to the acknowledgements after a conversation with the corresponding author. That conversation is much worse after publication."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Contributions"}</dt><dd>{"No CRediT statement. Drafted with the authors across the fourteen roles, which also settled a disagreement about author order that had been unresolved for two months."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The previous editor"}</dt><dd>{"Not acknowledged anywhere. Elsevier requires that anyone participating in substantive aspects such as language editing be recognised in the acknowledgements; Springer Nature and BMC require that and the funding source of the assistance. Added, naming both providers, including us."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"AI use"}</dt><dd>{"One author had used a language model to polish two paragraphs and had not mentioned it to anyone, including their co-authors. Declared, in the form the target publisher requires — which is not the same form at all four of the largest publishers."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Data availability"}</dt><dd>{"The statement offered more than the ethics approval permitted. Redrafted against the approval. An overpromised data statement is a problem you meet on the day somebody asks for the data."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Ethics and consent"}</dt><dd>{"Present, complete, correctly referenced. Recorded as passing, because a report that only lists faults is not a report."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · field, exposure and every figure changed"}</span><span>{"Editorial QC report, as delivered"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"One manuscript, already edited, checked against what was actually bought. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The level tab is the finding that should change how you buy."}</b>{" The previous provider did competent work — we kept 94% of their changes. They simply did not do the thing that was sold, and because no quote in this market names a level, the authors had no way of knowing. That is not one bad supplier; it is how the category is priced."}</p> <p><b>{"The checks tab carries the one nobody catches."}</b>{" A reference retracted eleven months earlier, still cited as current evidence. No copyedit finds it, no similarity report finds it, and no reference manager tells you. It only turns up if somebody opens every reference, which is a separate pass and takes an afternoon."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"The level named before the quote"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"In all three vocabularies, with what it excludes."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"A style sheet built and handed over"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Which is why terminology stops drifting."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Meaning never changed silently"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"“Associated with” does not become “led to” in an edit."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"References opened, not restyled"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Restyling propagates a wrong page range; reading catches a retraction."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a QC report built round a document like yours — same type, same discipline, same reporting guideline."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"Read the full QC report"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-eq"}> <span><b>{"Read the full QC report"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the level audit, the language findings, the reference and similarity checks, the declarations and what is handed over"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-eq"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Editorial and quality support · sample QC report"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Editorial QC report — observational cohort study, previously edited elsewhere"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real report with the field, the exposure, the institution, the other provider and every figure changed. The checks, the categories of finding and the reporting format are as delivered. Ask us and we will build one around a document like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"What was checked, and why this job existed"}</h4> <p>{"A 5,900-word observational cohort manuscript, returned from another provider’s highest editing tier, brought to us because the authors could not tell what had been done. That is the honest reason most of these jobs exist: an edited document looks edited, and nothing in it tells you which of the five levels you received."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"How it was handled"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Documents"}</td><td>{"The authors’ original, the returned edited version, the tracked-changes file and the previous provider’s invoice and scope description."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Level audit"}</td><td>{"Every change classified by the level of intervention it represents, so the delivered level could be stated rather than guessed."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reviewer"}</td><td>{"An editor in the discipline, plus a second reader who did not do the editing."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Language"}</td><td>{"A full line edit over the previous copyedit, keeping every earlier correction that was right."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"References"}</td><td>{"All 52 opened and read against the statements they support, and checked for retraction, expression of concern and indexing."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Similarity"}</td><td>{"Report run, and every match read and classified. Not scored."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reporting"}</td><td>{"STROBE mapped item by item to page and line."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Declarations"}</td><td>{"Authorship against the four ICMJE criteria, CRediT, interests, funding, ethics, consent, data availability and AI use."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"What this is not: peer review, and not a verdict on the previous provider’s competence. It is a statement of what was done to a document, measured against what was bought."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"The level audit — 1,184 changes, classified"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Level of intervention"}</th><th>{"Changes"}</th><th>{"What this tells you"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Mechanical: spelling, punctuation, articles, tense, number agreement"}</td><td><b>{"1,102"}</b></td><td>{"93% of the work. This is copyediting, and it was done well."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Sentence-level: splitting, reordering within a sentence, word choice"}</td><td><b>{"82"}</b></td><td>{"7%. Line editing happens at this level and this is not enough of it to constitute one."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Paragraph or section reordering"}</td><td><b>{"0"}</b></td><td>{"No structural work at all."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Queries raised to the authors"}</td><td><b>{"3"}</b></td><td>{"All three about a missing citation. None about a claim, a number or a method."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Changes that altered meaning"}</td><td><b>{"1"}</b></td><td>{"And it was made silently. See section 3."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Style sheet"}</td><td><b>{"None produced"}</b></td><td>{"Which is why the terminology drifts, and why the next paper from this project starts from nothing."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}><b>{"Delivered level: copyediting."}</b>{" Charged as premium scientific editing. We are not alleging bad faith — the invoice named a tier, not a level, and tiers are not defined anywhere in this market. There is no industry-standard taxonomy: the Editorial Freelancers Association names four services, the Chicago Manual of Style splits manuscript editing into mechanical and substantive and puts line editing before copyediting, and Editors Canada’s "}<i>{"Professional Editorial Standards"}</i>{" 2024 defines four levels under different names again. They do not map onto each other. Until a supplier tells you which of those things they will do, a quote is not comparable to any other quote."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The change that mattered"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Original"}</th><th>{"As returned by the previous editor"}</th><th>{"As we left it"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"“Exposure was associated with a higher rate of the outcome.”"}</td><td>{"“Exposure led to a significant increase in the outcome.”"}</td><td>{"“Exposure was associated with a higher rate of the outcome (adjusted HR 1.34, 95% CI 1.09 to 1.65).”"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p>{"The middle version reads better. It also asserts causation from an observational design, in the abstract, which is the objection this design always attracts and the fastest route to a reviewer deciding the authors do not understand their own study. It was made without a query, so the authors never saw the decision being taken."}</p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}><b>{"The rule this illustrates, and the one we work to:"}</b>{" an editor may change how a sentence reads without asking. An editor may not change what it claims without asking. Where the two conflict — and they conflict constantly in a discussion section — the claim wins and the query goes to the author. Our query log records every one of those decisions with its reasoning, which is also what makes answering a reviewer three months later a half-day rather than a week."}</p> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Language findings, over the top of a good copyedit"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Finding"}</th><th>{"Count"}</th><th>{"Resolution"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Earlier corrections kept"}</td><td>{"1,102 of 1,184"}</td><td>{"94%. They were right. An audit that rejects everything the previous supplier did is an audit selling itself rather than reporting."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Sentences over 45 words in the methods"}</td><td>{"11"}</td><td>{"Split where they contained more than one procedure. Grammatical length is not readable length."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Over-hedging"}</td><td>{"19"}</td><td>{"“It may possibly be suggested that there could be some indication of” reduced to the claim. Over-hedging costs authors more than overstatement, because a reviewer reads it as a lack of confidence in the work."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Terminology drift"}</td><td>{"3 variables, 2 abbreviations"}</td><td>{"Reconciled and recorded on a style sheet, which is handed over."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Unusual but clear constructions"}</td><td>{"Left alone"}</td><td>{"Two of four authors write in English as an additional language. The brief is clarity, not neutralisation, and a paper flattened into house prose has lost something it will not get back."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Further line-level changes"}</td><td>{"310"}</td><td>{"All tracked, all visible, 41 with a comment explaining why."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"The checks that are not editing"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Check"}</th><th>{"Result"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"References opened and read"}</td><td>{"52. "}<b>{"3"}</b>{" do not support the statement they are attached to — two inherited from another paper’s reference list, one supporting the opposite direction of effect in this population."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Retraction and expression of concern"}</td><td><b>{"1 retracted"}</b>{", eleven months before the manuscript was drafted, cited in the introduction as current evidence. Removed and the claim re-evidenced. No copyedit, similarity report or reference manager catches this."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Indexing"}</td><td>{"2 references from journals not indexed in any major database. Replaced."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Similarity report"}</td><td>{"34 matches, all read: "}<b>{"26"}</b>{" correctly quoted and cited methods text, "}<b>{"5"}</b>{" the authors’ own earlier methods needing citation as text recycling under COPE’s position of 20 August 2024, "}<b>{"2"}</b>{" needing a citation added, "}<b>{"1"}</b>{" a genuine attribution problem in the introduction, resolved with the authors. The overall percentage is not reported in our findings because it is not a finding — Turnitin states that plagiarism cannot be determined from the score alone and that there is no single acceptable score, and COPE advises against using any percentage as a benchmark."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reporting checklist"}</td><td>{"STROBE mapped. 22 items located by page and line; 4 incomplete, all answerable from documents the team held."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Numbers against tables"}</td><td>{"Every figure in the text checked against its source table. 2 mismatches, both in the abstract, both introduced in an earlier revision rather than by any editor."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"Declarations"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Declaration"}</th><th>{"What was done"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Authorship"}</td><td>{"Five authors listed. One met only the first ICMJE criterion — data collection, with no drafting, no recorded approval and no accountability. All four criteria must be met. Moved to the acknowledgements after a conversation with the corresponding author."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Contributions"}</td><td>{"No CRediT statement existed. Drafted with the authors across the fourteen roles of ANSI/NISO Z39.104-2022, which also settled an author-order disagreement that had been open for two months."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Editorial assistance"}</td><td>{"Neither provider was acknowledged. Elsevier requires that anyone participating in substantive aspects such as language editing or medical writing be recognised in the acknowledgements; Springer Nature and BMC require that plus the funding source, and warn that unacknowledged editorial services may constitute an undisclosed conflict of interest. Both providers named, including us."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"AI use"}</td><td>{"One author had used a language model on two paragraphs and had told nobody, including the co-authors. Declared in the form the target publisher requires. The four largest publishers differ on whether basic grammar tools are exempt and on where the declaration goes, so “we declared it” is not a complete answer without naming the publisher."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Data availability"}</td><td>{"The statement offered more than the ethics approval permitted. Redrafted against the approval."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Ethics, consent, funding, interests"}</td><td>{"All present, complete and correctly referenced. Recorded as passing."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"7"}</span>{"What was handed over"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Artefact"}</th><th>{"Why it matters afterwards"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"The edited document, tracked, and a clean version"}</td><td>{"Every change visible and rejectable. You approve an edit; you do not receive a new document."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The query log"}</td><td>{"Forty-one queries with our reasoning, including every point where a change would have altered a claim. It is the document that answers a reviewer three months later."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The style sheet"}</td><td>{"Every terminology, spelling and formatting decision. Yours, and the reason the next paper from this project costs less."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The reference log"}</td><td>{"All 52, what was checked, what was replaced and why, including the retraction."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The similarity reading"}</td><td>{"All 34 matches classified, with the action taken on each. Not a percentage."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The completed STROBE checklist"}</td><td>{"Mapped to page and line, ready to upload."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"A note on what we did not do"}</td><td>{"The shortest document in the pack and the one that prevents the next misunderstanding. We did not re-analyse the data, we did not assess whether the science is right, and we did not read the statistical code."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}><b>{"One thing this report deliberately does not contain:"}</b>{" a claim about what happens next. We do not guarantee journal acceptance, and an editorial QC report cannot. What it changes is whether a manuscript is judged on its science rather than discarded for a retracted citation, an unsupported causal verb in the abstract, or an authorship line that does not survive scrutiny — and those are worth buying on their own terms."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Benefits of naming the level first"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it changes, and what it cannot."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Editing does not make a study better. It stops a sound study being read as a careless one, and it stops you paying four times over for a level you did not receive."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"A quote you can actually compare"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The level named in all three published vocabularies, with what it excludes. Publishing the scope is what makes the quote comparable at all, which is the whole point of printing it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"You are told when a cheaper level will do"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The free sample edit is partly for you and partly for us: it is how we find out that a document asking for a substantive edit needs a copyedit. That conversation costs us money often enough to be worth mentioning."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Meaning is never changed silently"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"An editor may change how a sentence reads without asking. An editor may not change what it claims without asking. Every one of those decisions is a query with reasoning, and the log is yours."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The checks that editing does not include"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"References opened rather than restyled, retractions caught, the reporting checklist mapped, the similarity report read rather than scored. Separate passes, because each finds what the others miss."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-packages-1adzr7j"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four levels, all priced at the same length, so you can compare them."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Editing is commonly sold as Standard, Advanced and Premium, with only one of the three carrying a price and none of them saying which level of editing it actually is — which is the defect this whole page is about. These four are the levels themselves, all costed at 6,000 words — a normal research manuscript — so the ladder is visible rather than implied. Longer or shorter documents are the same rate per word, and the chooser above will do the arithmetic."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers tiers--4 rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Proofread"}</span> <h3>{"The last read before it goes"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Documents that are already right, and typeset proofs coming back from a publisher"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $150"}</b><span>{"6,000 words · $0.025/word · minimum $110"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"2–4 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Typographical errors, spelling, spacing, running heads"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Figure, table and equation numbering and cross-references"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Anything introduced by typesetting, checked against the previous stage"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A final consistency read on a manuscript rather than a proof"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"It does not touch sentences, structure or references. If a paragraph is hard to follow, this returns it hard to follow and correctly spelled."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Proofread"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Copyedit"}</span> <h3>{"Correct, consistent and to house style"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Drafts where the writing works and the mechanics, terminology and references do not"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $210"}</b><span>{"6,000 words · $0.035/word · minimum $160"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"3–6 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Grammar, usage, punctuation and spelling"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Terminology and abbreviations made consistent, on a style sheet you keep"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reference styling and completeness, and every cross-reference checked"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Journal house style, figure and table numbering"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Tracked changes with a query where a change would alter meaning"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"It does not rewrite for clarity. A copyedit makes a manuscript correct, not persuasive."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Copyedit"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Line edit"}</span> <h3>{"Sentence by sentence, in your voice"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Drafts that are correct and hard to read — the level most authors need and least often buy"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $300"}</b><span>{"6,000 words · $0.050/word · copyediting included"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"5–8 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Copyedit, not billed twice"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Clarity, flow and register, sentence by sentence"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Paragraph order within a section; redundancy removed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Hedging that hides a finding, and overstatement that inflates one"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Your voice kept — unusual and clear is left alone"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"It does not reorder sections or rebuild an argument. If the discussion claims more than the results support, that is the level above."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Line edit"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Substantive"}</span> <h3>{"Structure, argument and the full QC"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Drafts where the writing is not the problem, and documents already edited elsewhere"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $450"}</b><span>{"6,000 words · $0.075/word · all lower levels included"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7–12 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Line edit, at document scale"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Section order and balance; the introduction narrowed to one question"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every number in the text checked against the table it came from"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every claim measured against the result it rests on"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reporting checklist mapped to page and line; references opened and read"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Declarations reviewed; similarity report read rather than scored"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Developmental editing — rebuilding rather than improving — is $0.100 a word and starts with a plan you approve before any rewriting."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-eq"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-eq"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Substantive"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"psv rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The query log"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Every query"}</b><span>{"with the reasoning"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Including every change we did "}<i>{"not"}</i>{" make"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Where a change would have altered what the document claims, it is a query rather than an edit, and the query carries our reasoning. It is also the document that makes answering a reviewer three months later a half-day rather than a week."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The style sheet"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"One page"}</b><span>{"every decision recorded"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Terminology, spelling, abbreviations, format"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Built before the editing starts and handed over at the end. It is what stops terminology drifting across a long document, what lets a second editor work without contradicting the first, and what makes the next paper from the same project cheaper."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The reference log"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Each one"}</b><span>{"opened, not matched"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"With retractions and indexing checked"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Every reference read against the statement it supports, with what was replaced and why. It is the pass that catches a paper retracted eighteen months ago and still cited as current — which no copyedit, similarity report or reference manager will tell you about."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Priced alongside any level: developmental editing at $0.100 a word; reference verification as a standalone pass; similarity report read and classified; reporting-guideline mapping on its own; declarations and authorship review; journal reformatting for a resubmission; figure and table preparation; translation review against a source text; and expedited delivery where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than on urgency. Institutional and publisher arrangements are quoted per title or per cohort rather than per document."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-guarantee-1jjfynq"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"One thing worth stating plainly: we do not guarantee journal acceptance. Everything else here is the detail behind it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the document meets the level agreed, with no cap on rounds inside that scope, and the editor available when the reviewers or the supervisor come back rather than reassigned."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The level is in writing before you pay"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Named in the EFA, Chicago and Editors Canada vocabularies, with what it excludes. If what arrives is not that level, it is our cost to put right."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Meaning changes only with a query"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Every point where an edit would alter what the document claims is a question to you, with the estimate or the evidence it rests on, recorded in the log."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"A second reader, always"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Somebody who did not do the editing reads it before it comes back. An editor re-reading their own work reads what they intended to write."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A change that introduced an error, a reference not opened, a guideline version wrong — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We do not guarantee journal acceptance, we do not influence editorial decisions, and we have no relationship with any editor or reviewer that could affect one. We do not sell similarity reduction — we read the report and tell you what each match is, and where a passage needs a citation we say so rather than rewording it to lower a number. We do not sell AI-detection clearance: the published false-positive rates make that impossible to offer honestly, and they fall hardest on exactly the authors who would buy it. We do not issue certificates as evidence of anything; no publisher we could find requires one, treats one as bearing on a decision, or rejects a paper for lacking one, and the “Scopus-accepted” and “Web of Science ready” certificates advertised in this market correspond to no scheme either organisation runs — we will instead confirm in writing exactly what we did, which is the thing an institution may actually require. We are not peer reviewers and this is not peer review. We will not edit assessed work where an institution’s regulations prohibit assistance. And we will not quietly improve a claim your evidence does not support: we will query it, show you what it rests on, and if you want it as written, restore it and record that we advised against it."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"A thousand words edited free, before anything is agreed"}</p> <p>{"Not a sample of somebody else’s work — yours, edited, so you can see the level of intervention and the tone we take with your voice before you commit to anything. It also protects you from the failure this page is about: we find out whether the level you asked for is the level the document needs, and if it needs less we quote less. Two business days, no cost, no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Your unpublished work stays yours"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and editors and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data, drafts, decision letters and supervisor correspondence are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015 — certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N — kept only as long as the project needs them and never used to train anything. We do not reuse your text on anyone else’s project and we do not publish your work as a sample: every sample on this site is redacted or composite."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Declared, not ghosted"}</p> <p>{"Our involvement goes in your acknowledgements, naming the company and what we did. The ICMJE is explicit that writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading do not confer authorship; Elsevier requires that such contributors be recognised; Springer Nature and BMC require that plus the funding source, and warn that unacknowledged editorial services may constitute an undisclosed conflict of interest. Where you used another supplier before us, they belong in the acknowledgement too, and we will say so."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Your voice, not our house style"}</p> <p>{"The brief is clarity, not neutralisation. Where a construction is unusual and clear, it stays. This matters most for authors writing in an additional language, who are the largest group buying editing and the group most often handed back a paper that reads like every other paper — correct, fluent, and no longer theirs. Where we do impose consistency it is recorded on the style sheet, which is yours, so you can see every decision and reverse any of them."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-client-stories-1exnw4j"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three documents, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing. Nothing here claims a publication outcome, because an editorial service does not produce one."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They told us the previous editor had done a copyedit, not the tier we paid for, and showed us the change counts.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"COHORT"}<br />{"STUDY"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Editorial"}<br />{"QC"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Research fellow · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"QC report and substantive edit"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Our similarity score had frightened us for a week. They read all thirty-four matches and twenty-six were our own correctly cited methods.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"MANUSCRIPT"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Similarity"}<br />{"Read"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Associate professor · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Similarity reading and copyedit"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They queried a sentence instead of improving it. The improved version would have claimed causation from a cohort study.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"THESIS"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Line"}<br />{"Edit"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Doctoral candidate · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Line edit, style sheet and query log"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-editorial-quality-support-faq-1r4unno"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Editorial and quality support FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Ten questions clients ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure which level you need? Send the document and we will edit a thousand words of it free and tell you. "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-0"}><span>{"What types of documents do you support?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Journal manuscripts of every design; systematic reviews and meta-analyses; case reports; theses and dissertations; grant applications and research proposals; book chapters and scholarly reports; regulatory and clinical documents; and institutional or publisher work at volume. Across medicine and the health sciences, the life sciences, engineering and computing, psychology and the social sciences, economics and management, and the humanities. We also take documents that have already been edited somewhere else — that is frequently the most useful thing we do, and section four of the sample report on this page is exactly that job."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-1"}><span>{"Do you guarantee acceptance in journals?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-1"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"No."}</b>{" The answer that was already on this page is the right one and we have kept it: while we bring a manuscript up to high editorial and formatting standards, we do not guarantee journal acceptance. Acceptance is an editorial decision, made by people we have no relationship with, about science we did not do. It is worth adding what the published evidence says about why editing helps less than the market implies: in the best-documented analysis of reviewer comments, the leading reasons for rejection were statistical problems, overinterpretation, inappropriate instrumentation and sample size, with “text difficult to follow” ranking fifth. Editing reaches the fifth-ranked problem well and the first four not at all. Note also that no publisher-affiliated editing service claims otherwise — the strongest promise any of them makes is a free re-edit or a refund, not an outcome."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-2"}><span>{"What similarity score is acceptable?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-2"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"There is no acceptable score, because the score is not a measure of plagiarism."}</b>{" Turnitin’s own guidance says so in almost those words: “plagiarism cannot be determined by the similarity score alone”, the number is “simply the percentage of text in a submission that matches other sources”, and there is “no single ‘acceptable’ or ‘perfect’ Similarity score”. A correctly quoted, correctly cited passage raises the number exactly as a copied one does. "}<b>{"Nor is there a published threshold."}</b>{" COPE states that it “does not recommend using a specific percentage of duplication or overlap as a benchmark”. Elsevier tells its editors a high score does not necessarily indicate plagiarised text. Springer Nature publishes bands for "}<i>{"editors"}</i>{" — screen quickly above 10%, check carefully above 20% — and says explicitly that individual source scores matter more than the overall index. The “under 15%” figure that circulates widely traces to no publisher, no guideline and no primary source we could find. What we do is read every match and tell you which need a citation, which are your own earlier work and need handling as text recycling, and which are a real problem."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-3"}><span>{"Can you make sure my paper passes an AI detector?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and we would not take your money for trying. Seven GPT detectors tested on human-written TOEFL essays produced an average "}<b>{"61.3% false-positive rate"}</b>{", and "}<b>{"19.8%"}</b>{" of those essays were called AI-generated by every detector, while essays by native-English school students were classified almost perfectly (Liang et al., "}<i>{"Patterns"}</i>{", 2023). The tools key on text perplexity, so they penalise writing with less lexical variety — which means they systematically penalise the authors most likely to buy reassurance about them. Turnitin’s own claims have moved a long way from the “98% confidence” of its 2023 launch: it now publishes no headline accuracy figure, does not surface results below 20%, warns that submissions under 300 words are unreliable, and states that a score “should not be used as the sole basis for adverse actions”. COPE’s September 2025 guidance is the line to hold: detection tools “should not be relied upon in isolation”. What we will do is help you write an accurate declaration of whatever AI you actually used, in the form your publisher requires."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-4"}><span>{"Which level of editing do I need?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Use the chooser above, then send the document and we will confirm it by editing a thousand words free. The short version: if the problem is typographical, "}<b>{"proofreading"}</b>{". If it is grammar, terminology and references, "}<b>{"copyediting"}</b>{". If the sentences are correct and hard to read, "}<b>{"line editing"}</b>{" — the level most authors need and least often buy. If the structure or the argument is wrong, "}<b>{"substantive editing"}</b>{". If the document needs rebuilding rather than improving, "}<b>{"developmental editing"}</b>{", which starts with a plan you approve before any rewriting. The reason this question is hard is that there is no industry-standard taxonomy: the Editorial Freelancers Association names four services, the Chicago Manual of Style splits manuscript editing into mechanical and substantive at 2.49 and 2.50 and treats line editing as an earlier separate pass, and Editors Canada’s "}<i>{"Professional Editorial Standards"}</i>{" 2024 defines four levels under different names again. They do not map onto each other, which is why two honest quotes can differ fourfold."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-5"}><span>{"Who will edit my document?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"An editor working in your subject area, matched to the document type as well as the discipline — a thesis editor and a regulatory editor are different people, and so are a copyeditor and a developmental editor. Then a second reader who did not do the editing, on every job at every level, because an editor re-reading their own work reads what they intended rather than what is on the page. You are told who is doing it, and the same editor stays with the document through revisions and is available when the reviewers or your supervisor come back. Where a document needs a level we cannot staff properly in your field, we say so and decline rather than assigning somebody who will learn the subject on your manuscript."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-6"}><span>{"Will you change what my paper says?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Not without asking. The rule we work to is that an editor may change how a sentence reads without asking and may not change what it claims without asking — and in a discussion section those two things conflict constantly. Where they do, the claim wins and the query goes to you, with the estimate or the evidence the sentence rests on attached. The sample report on this page includes a real example of the failure: another provider turned “was associated with” into “led to” in an abstract. It reads better and it asserts causation from an observational cohort, which is the objection that design always attracts. It was made without a query, so the authors never saw the decision being taken. Every one of our queries, and the reasoning behind it, is in a log you keep."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-7"}><span>{"Do you provide a certificate of editing?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"We provide written confirmation of exactly what was done, at what level, on what date — which is useful, and which your institution may require for a declaration. We do not market it as an editing certificate, because certificates in this market are sold as though they carry editorial weight and they do not. "}<b>{"No publisher we checked requires one, treats one as bearing on a decision, or rejects a paper for lacking one."}</b>{" The only publisher-side mention we found is MDPI, which says that if you use a service that issues a confirmation certificate you may send a copy to the editorial office — permissive, with no stated effect. Publishers’ own editing arms sell certificates too, and are careful about what they promise: Springer Nature’s guarantee alongside its certificate is a free re-edit if a paper is rejected for the English alone, not acceptance. Treat the “Scopus-accepted” and “Web of Science ready” certificates advertised in this market with suspicion: neither organisation operates any such scheme."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-8"}><span>{"Can you edit my thesis, and do I have to declare it?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Sometimes, and the answer is your institution’s rather than ours. Universities differ sharply: some permit language editing within stated limits, some require a declaration naming the editor and the work done, some prohibit third-party assistance in assessed work entirely. "}<b>{"Send us the regulations before you send us the thesis."}</b>{" Where help is permitted we work inside the limits — which usually means language and consistency but not structure or argument — and give you written confirmation of exactly what was done so your declaration is accurate. Where it is prohibited, we decline, and we will not help anyone work around it. For journal articles the position is different and simpler: we found no publisher that prohibits professional editing, and all the major ones require only that it be acknowledged, with Springer Nature and BMC also asking for the funding source of the assistance."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"eq-9"}><span>{"How do you handle confidentiality?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"eq-9"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and editors and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data, drafts, decision letters and supervisor correspondence are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N, kept only as long as the project needs them and never used to train anything. We do not reuse your text on anyone else’s project, and we do not publish your work as a sample — every sample on this site is redacted or composite. A document Pubrica holds is confidential whoever wrote it, so the sample on this page names neither the client nor the earlier editor, and never will."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of an edit."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Writing it, checking it before an editor sees it, and preparing it for the journal."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"IF IT IS NOT WRITTEN YET"}</b><em>{"writing rather than editing"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/scientific-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Scientific and academic writing"}</b><span>{"Written with you from your data, when editing is not the right purchase."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical writing"}</b><span>{"The clinical and regulatory side of the same discipline."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"CHECKS BEYOND EDITING"}</b><em>{"science, not sentences"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"A reviewer’s objection, before an editor makes it."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/plagiarism-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Plagiarism and AI authorship check"}</b><span>{"The report read and classified rather than delivered as a number."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"GETTING IT OUT"}</b><em>{"format and submit"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-manuscript-formatting-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Manuscript formatting"}</b><span>{"To the journal’s own specification, including the awkward parts."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/responding-to-reviewers/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Response to reviewer comments"}</b><span>{"Point by point, built from the query log we handed you."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on getting published."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces on the funder rules that now shape where an edited paper can go."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/nih-public-access-policy-2025/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"NIH Public Access Policy 2025: what changed"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"The twelve-month embargo is gone. What that means for where NIH-funded work can be submitted, and when."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/horizon-europe-article-processing-charges/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"Horizon Europe will not pay a hybrid journal APC"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"A funding rule that removes a large number of journals from the shortlist before scope is even considered."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/japan-immediate-open-access/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"Japan’s immediate open access rule from FY2025"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"What the requirement covers, which outputs it reaches, and how it changes journal selection."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the document. We will edit a thousand words of it free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"You see the level of intervention and the tone we take with your voice; we find out which level the document actually needs. Two business days, no cost, no obligation — and if it needs less than you asked for, that is what we will quote."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
